{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch252RirQ2KVQM6FYNiHR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm not signing off: the sort direction bug is still there, and I found a second suspected problem with note links that the developer also could not reproduce.\n\n**Bug filed (one report, plus repeat attempts):**\n- **Sort direction ignored for \"By title\".** With Sorting set to \"By title\", the list and subtasks stay A→Z whether the direction reads Ascending or Descending. Reproduced several times: before and after closing the sheet, and after a portrait/landscape rotation. \"By due date\" does respond to direction. Subtasks by title show the same behaviour (Charge phone, Print tickets in both directions).\n- The developer replied \"could not reproduce with the steps given\" to my first report and to a re-filed version with more detail. I didn't file the subtask case separately because I expect it's the same cause.\n\n**Not filed, developer disputed:** the note link \"See https://example.com/guide\" on Read docs shows as plain grey text in the list, with no link styling and no way to open it from the list. Tapping the row opens the editor. The developer couldn't reproduce this either. I didn't reopen it, so the link-detection question is unresolved.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- The Sort sheet keeps its values after closing and reopening, and the list reflects them.\n- Due-date group headers match the expected dates: Thursday (Nov 19), Tuesday Nov 24, Friday Dec 4, and \"No due date\". When grouping is None, the date labels read \"Thu\", \"Nov 24\" and \"Dec 4\".\n- Due-date ascending order: Buy milk, Pack for trip, Pay rent, Read docs.\n- Subtasks by title ascending: Charge phone, then Print tickets.\n- Choosing a Subtasks option resets its direction to Ascending (By due date). I didn't treat this as a bug, since it may be intended.\n\n**Not covered:** the grouping options beyond None and due date (start date, priority, list), any completion or undo flows, and the link behaviour inside the editor."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4128, "cache_read_input_tokens": 105938, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4128}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "fe434278-2b0f-450c-b55a-258fc273a7fd", "uuid": "bd174813-b65b-40ed-a947-5f48a9e642c4", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T02:57:48.320Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch252RUDWCviCXGCS8pQU"}
